{"file_path":"crates/tldr-cli/src/commands/daemon/watcher.rs","language":"rust","docstring":"In-daemon filesystem watcher (TLDR-ac0.2).\n\nBrings file-change detection INTO the Rust daemon, co-located with the\nin-RAM index it mutates, replacing the cross-process C++ fsnotifier → IPC\n`Notify` hop. The shape is:\n\n```text\nnotify OS watcher (own thread, raw accepted events)\n│  watch_decision() filter (cheap excludes + corpus membership)\n▼\nbounded mpsc<PathBuf>   ── overflow flag (never block the watch thread)\n▼\nfixed-window collector ── five-second window + rolling burst cap\n▼\nbounded mpsc<Batch>\n▼\nsingle serialized batch executor\n│\n└─ batch delta OR one single-flight full rebuild\n```\n\nThe watcher and worker share NO lock — invalidation flows over the channel,\ndissolving the async-thread-mutex hazard (TLDR-qr9) by construction. Honest\nframing: notify is NOT faster than fsnotifier (same OS primitives); the win\nis consolidation into one process and making the t8f delta an in-process\ncall rather than an IPC contract.","imports":[{"module":"std::collections","names":["HashSet","VecDeque"],"is_from":true},{"module":"std::future","names":["Future"],"is_from":true},{"module":"std::path","names":["Path","PathBuf"],"is_from":true},{"module":"std::sync::atomic","names":["AtomicBool","Ordering"],"is_from":true},{"module":"std::sync","names":["Arc"],"is_from":true},{"module":"std::time","names":["Duration","Instant"],"is_from":true},{"module":"notify_debouncer_full::notify","names":["recommended_watcher","Event","EventKind","RecommendedWatcher","RecursiveMode","Watcher"],"is_from":true},{"module":"tokio::sync","names":["mpsc"],"is_from":true},{"module":"tldr_core::semantic","names":["is_corpus_file","store_dir_for"],"is_from":true},{"module":"tldr_core::walker","names":["build_path_ignore_matcher","PathIgnoreMatcher","TLDRIGNORE_FILE"],"is_from":true},{"module":"super::activity","names":["ActivityTracker","Source"],"is_from":true},{"module":"super::daemon","names":["TLDRDaemon"],"is_from":true},{"module":"tests","is_from":false}],"functions":[{"name":"watch_decision","params":["project","cache_excl","store_dir","ignore_matcher","path","kind"],"return_type":"bool","docstring":"Decide whether a single event path should be enqueued for reindexing.\n\n\n\nPure and side-effect-free (modulo the filesystem reads it performs) so the\n\ntrap / corpus / symlink tests can exercise it directly without standing up a\n\nlive daemon and racing debounce timing.\n\n\n\nOrder of checks (cheapest first, and the prefix excludes are load-bearing\n\nfor DELETES — see below):\n\n1. Pure read events (`Access`) carry no index change → drop.\n\n2. The daemon's OWN writes must never feed back: the in-tree `<root>/.tldr`\n\n   cache subtree (`persist_stats` writes `salsa_stats.json` there) and the\n\n   resident store dir. A prefix check is the ONLY self-write defense that\n\n   works for deletes — `is_corpus_file` canonicalizes the file and so always\n\n   returns `false` for a vanished path, which would otherwise let a deleted\n\n   `.tldr/*` file fall through to the passthrough branch.\n\n3. `.tldrignore` / `.gitignore` exclusion (TLDR-1j2): consulted via the\n\n   root-level `ignore_matcher` BEFORE the `exists()` branch so it ALSO drops\n\n   DELETES inside ignored dirs (a vanished path can't be walked). For paths\n\n   that still exist, the deeper per-directory matching is handled by\n\n   `is_corpus_file` in step 4; this matcher is the only mechanism that can\n\n   drop a deleted ignored file before a wasted southbound reindex hop.\n\n4. An existing path must be a corpus member (same walker rules as the build,\n\n   `.tldrignore`-aware via `add_custom_ignore_filename`).\n\n5. A vanished path (delete / rename-away) that survived the ignore matcher is\n\n   passed through; `apply_delta`'s store-side delete filter cleanly drops it\n\n   (`removed == 0` → `Filtered`) if it was never indexed.\n","is_method":false,"is_async":false,"line":280,"line_end":305},{"name":"presence_decision","params":["cache_excl","store_dir","path","kind"],"return_type":"bool","docstring":"Decide whether a single event counts as project PRESENCE for the daemon's\n\nidle timer (TLDR-3w5) — deliberately looser than [`watch_decision`]: a\n\n`cargo build` writing to `target/` is filtered from indexing (not corpus)\n\nbut is still proof someone is alive in this project, so liveness taps the\n\nevent stream BEFORE the corpus filter.\n\n\n\nTwo exclusions, both immortality-safe by design (a daemon must never count\n\nits own activity as presence):\n\n- Self-writes (`<root>/.tldr` cache subtree + resident store dir): counting\n\n  our own store/stats writes would be a self-perpetuating liveness loop.\n\n- `Access` (read) events — INTENTIONAL, do not \"restore\" raw-event\n\n  behavior: the daemon's own corpus READS during build/delta (plus\n\n  Spotlight/backup/AV scanners) fire `Access` events, which would make an\n\n  actively-building daemon immortal via its own reads. Writes-only loses\n\n  nothing the presence philosophy wants — human/agent/build activity\n\n  manifests as `Modify`/`Create`/`Remove`.\n","is_method":false,"is_async":false,"line":323,"line_end":332},{"name":"spawn_watcher","params":["daemon"],"return_type":"Option<WatcherGuard>","docstring":"Spawn the recursive project watcher and its serialized reindex worker.\n\n\n\nReturns the guard to hold for the daemon's lifetime (see [`WatcherGuard`]).\n\nReturns `None` — and the daemon keeps serving the IPC `Notify` path — if the\n\nhard self-write precondition fails or the OS watcher can't be created; both\n\nare logged. Must be called from within a Tokio runtime (it spawns the\n\nworker task).\n","is_method":false,"is_async":false,"line":341,"line_end":431},{"name":"run_pipeline_worker","params":["rx","batch_tx","overflowed","config"],"is_method":false,"is_async":true,"line":433,"line_end":477},{"name":"accept_signal","params":["batch_tx","pipeline","rx","signal"],"return_type":"bool","is_method":false,"is_async":true,"line":479,"line_end":497},{"name":"drain_receiver","params":["rx"],"is_method":false,"is_async":false,"line":499,"line_end":501},{"name":"dispatch_flush","params":["daemon","flush"],"is_method":false,"is_async":true,"line":503,"line_end":510},{"name":"drain_batches_serially","params":["rx","dispatch"],"is_method":false,"is_async":true,"line":512,"line_end":520},{"name":"config","params":[],"return_type":"WatchPipelineConfig","is_method":false,"is_async":false,"decorators":["cfg(test)/* via mod tests */","cfg(test)"],"line":536,"line_end":543},{"name":"ignore_policy_reloads_during_a_live_session","params":[],"is_method":false,"is_async":false,"decorators":["test","cfg(test)/* via mod tests */","cfg(test)"],"line":546,"line_end":570},{"name":"ignore_policy_ordinary_source_event_does_not_reload","params":[],"is_method":false,"is_async":false,"decorators":["test","cfg(test)/* via mod tests */","cfg(test)"],"line":573,"line_end":580},{"name":"nested_ignore_policy_reloads_during_a_live_session","params":[],"is_method":false,"is_async":false,"decorators":["test","cfg(test)/* via mod tests */","cfg(test)"],"line":583,"line_end":608},{"name":"ignore_policy_event_enqueues_full_rebuild","params":[],"is_method":false,"is_async":false,"decorators":["test","cfg(test)/* via mod tests */","cfg(test)"],"line":611,"line_end":630},{"name":"ordinary_source_event_enqueues_path_delta","params":[],"is_method":false,"is_async":false,"decorators":["test","cfg(test)/* via mod tests */","cfg(test)"],"line":633,"line_end":652},{"name":"repeated_saves_to_one_file_coalesce_to_one_delta","params":[],"is_method":false,"is_async":false,"decorators":["test","cfg(test)/* via mod tests */","cfg(test)"],"line":655,"line_end":677},{"name":"fixed_window_includes_events_until_five_second_deadline","params":[],"is_method":false,"is_async":false,"decorators":["test","cfg(test)/* via mod tests */","cfg(test)"],"line":680,"line_end":699},{"name":"watcher_batches_queue_while_indexing_and_execute_serially","params":[],"is_method":false,"is_async":true,"decorators":["tokio::test","cfg(test)/* via mod tests */","cfg(test)"],"line":702,"line_end":753},{"name":"steady_stream_flushes_at_first_event_max_wait","params":[],"is_method":false,"is_async":false,"decorators":["test","cfg(test)/* via mod tests */","cfg(test)"],"line":756,"line_end":778},{"name":"later_events_do_not_rearm_the_fixed_window","params":[],"is_method":false,"is_async":false,"decorators":["test","cfg(test)/* via mod tests */","cfg(test)"],"line":781,"line_end":801},{"name":"file_cap_escalates_and_clears_pending_deltas","params":[],"is_method":false,"is_async":false,"decorators":["test","cfg(test)/* via mod tests */","cfg(test)"],"line":804,"line_end":822},{"name":"rolling_event_cap_spans_fixed_window_flushes","params":[],"is_method":false,"is_async":false,"decorators":["test","cfg(test)/* via mod tests */","cfg(test)"],"line":825,"line_end":846}],"classes":[{"name":"WatchPipelineConfig","methods":[{"name":"from_daemon","params":["daemon"],"return_type":"Self","is_method":true,"is_async":false,"line":68,"line_end":76}],"fields":[{"name":"max_wait","field_type":"Duration","is_static":false,"is_constant":false,"visibility":"private","line":61,"line_end":61},{"name":"burst_file_cap","field_type":"usize","is_static":false,"is_constant":false,"visibility":"private","line":62,"line_end":62},{"name":"burst_event_cap","field_type":"usize","is_static":false,"is_constant":false,"visibility":"private","line":63,"line_end":63},{"name":"burst_window","field_type":"Duration","is_static":false,"is_constant":false,"visibility":"private","line":64,"line_end":64}],"line":60,"line_end":65},{"name":"Flush","methods":[],"line":80,"line_end":83},{"name":"WatchSignal","methods":[],"line":86,"line_end":89},{"name":"WatchPipeline","docstring":"Deterministic worker-owned debounce and rolling-burst state.\n\n\n\nThe notify thread only enqueues accepted paths. Keeping all timing state in\n\none serialized owner makes quiet/max-wait ordering explicit and prevents a\n\nmutex from leaking onto notify's synchronous callback thread.\n","methods":[{"name":"new","params":["config"],"return_type":"Self","is_method":true,"is_async":false,"line":104,"line_end":111},{"name":"accept","params":["&mut self","path","now"],"return_type":"Option<Flush>","is_method":true,"is_async":false,"line":113,"line_end":132},{"name":"deadline","params":["&self"],"return_type":"Option<Instant>","is_method":true,"is_async":false,"line":134,"line_end":141},{"name":"flush_due","params":["&mut self","now"],"return_type":"Option<Flush>","is_method":true,"is_async":false,"line":143,"line_end":151},{"name":"reset_all","params":["&mut self"],"is_method":true,"is_async":false,"line":153,"line_end":157}],"fields":[{"name":"config","field_type":"WatchPipelineConfig","is_static":false,"is_constant":false,"visibility":"private","line":97,"line_end":97},{"name":"pending","field_type":"HashSet<PathBuf>","is_static":false,"is_constant":false,"visibility":"private","line":98,"line_end":98},{"name":"first_event","field_type":"Option<Instant>","is_static":false,"is_constant":false,"visibility":"private","line":99,"line_end":99},{"name":"accepted_events","field_type":"VecDeque<Instant>","is_static":false,"is_constant":false,"visibility":"private","line":100,"line_end":100}],"line":96,"line_end":101},{"name":"LiveIgnoreMatcher","methods":[{"name":"new","params":["project"],"return_type":"Self","is_method":true,"is_async":false,"line":166,"line_end":171},{"name":"reload_for_paths","params":["&self","paths"],"return_type":"bool","is_method":true,"is_async":false,"line":173,"line_end":184},{"name":"snapshot","params":["&self"],"return_type":"Option<PathIgnoreMatcher>","is_method":true,"is_async":false,"line":186,"line_end":188},{"name":"is_ignored","params":["&self","path","is_dir"],"return_type":"bool","is_method":true,"is_async":false,"decorators":["cfg(test)"],"line":191,"line_end":196}],"fields":[{"name